riterion":"A library `show_ticket` with `REBAR_ROOT` unset, run from inside a git work tree, starts at most 1 `rev-parse --show-toplevel`, shown by a git-spawn-count test.","kind":"codebase-verifiable","met":true},{"citation":{"description":"test_a_cwd_change_between_reads_resolves_the_new_root chdirs between two repos and asserts the new root is returned. test_a_repo_created_inside_a_cached_root_is_resolved covers the nested-repo case. The cache key includes cwd, and _toplevel_still_valid (_config_sources.py 101-118) re-validates each hit.","kind":"file","line_end":247,"line_start":220,"path":"tests/unit/test_read_freshness_git_spawns.py"},"criterion":"A cwd change between reads still resolves the new cwd's repo root, shown by a test.","kind":"codebase-verifiable","met":true},{"citation":{"description":"repo_root returns early for an explicit arg or REBAR_ROOT. Otherwise it serves a cached toplevel when _toplevel_still_valid passes, and only then runs git rev-parse. Entries are re-checked by stat on every hit, and a failed lookup pops the entry. This removes the repeated per-read git spawns, since tracker_dir and load_config both go through repo_root.","kind":"file","line_end":98,"line_start":67,"path":"src/rebar/_config_sources.py"},"criterion":"Bug is actually resolved: library reads no longer rediscover the repo root with git on every call when REBAR_ROOT is unset.","kind":"codebase-verifiable","met":true}],"findings":[],"material_basis":"unpinned_completion_inputs","material_fingerprint":"4a2a09a983f2f360","metrics":{"alias_index_build_ms":2940,"commits_inspected":3710,"descendant_ids":0,"descendant_scope_ms":9869,"det_ms":20051.1,"diff_validation_ms":43,"distinct_references":3218,"git_history_read_ms":127,"landing_check_ms":3166,"llm_calls":1,"llm_ms":13579.3,"material_policy_ms":0,"pre_verifier_total_ms":30675,"referencing_commits_found":1,"requests":2,"structural_scan_ms":10136,"ticket_ref_resolution_ms":50,"tool_calls":1,"total_ms":33721.8,"verifier_annotat